        "Content": "A Beautifully presented and flexible detached 4 Bedroom House extending to approximately 198 Sq. m (2,131 Sq. ft).\r\n\r\nThis pristine residence is very conveniently located and is set on 0.23 Hec (0.57 Acre) of private grounds at the idyllic rural setting yet so convenient for access to Clonakilty Town and the N71 to Cork City.\r\n\r\nThe property itself is a two storey double fronted house with countryside views and mature garden areas. The house provides open plan living combined with flexible breakout rooms suitable for modern family living.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises of a Porch, Reception Hall, Living Room, Kitchen/Dining Room, Sun Room, Utility Room, wc,  Bathroom, Flexible Room (Sitting Room/Bedroom/Playroom, Hot Press with storage and a double bedroom with ensuite on the ground floor.\r\n\r\nThe first floor contains an impressive and spacious Master Bedroom, complete with an en-suite bathroom and a large walk-in wardrobe. There are two further rooms on this level, one of which is currently utilised as a dressing room, while the other benefits from its own en-suite bathroom.\r\n\r\nThe residence has a wonderful curb appeal with a gravel drive flanked by mature trees and hedges. There is plenty of private car parking. There is a large garden laid out with grass, a garden shed, green house and a raised garden area suitable for planting.\r\n\r\nThe property has a lovely private situation yet is very convenient to access. It is only 5 minutes to Clonakilty and 2 minutes to the N71 National Road which connects Cork City with Bandon, Clonakilty and all the way west to Kenmare in Co. Kerry.\r\n\r\nCork International Airport is 50 minutes away and Cork City Centre 55 minutes.\r\n\r\nThe vibrant heritage town of Clonakilty is renowned for its welcoming community and excellent range of amenities, including schools, healthcare services, supermarkets, boutique shops, cafés, award-winning restaurants, hotels and a wealth of independent local businesses.\r\n\r\nThe surrounding coastline is one of West Cork’s greatest attractions, with numerous beautiful beaches and scenic destinations close by, including Inchydoney, Long Strand, Owenahincha, The Warren, Blind Strand, Broadstrand, Dunneen Beach, Red Strand and the wonderful walking trails through Castlefreke Woods to name a few.\r\n\r\nFeatures–\r\n\r\nMains Water\r\n\r\nPrivate Drainage\r\n\r\nOil Fired Central Heating System\r\n\r\nFully Alarmed and with Security Cameras\r\n\r\nP85 FN77 (Property Specific Code)\r\n\r\nViewing Is Highly Recommended – Strictly By Appointment Only\r\n\r\nDisclaimer: All information provided is to the best of our knowledge but is not guaranteed and should be independently verified. No warranties or representations are made regarding the accuracy, completeness, condition or planning status of the property. Interested parties should satisfy themselves as to the correctness of all information provided, including measurements, boundaries, size or acreage, BER details and services. All measurements and distances are approximate and for guidance only. Photographs and video are for illustrative purposes and may include items not included in the sale (e.g. furniture)."
